Animate lockscreen widgets with their lock surface's animation manager.

Each lockscreen widget had an animation manager of its own, which the lock
surface's frame loop never looks at: it only ran frame ticks for the
surface's own animations, so a widget animation never advanced unless the
widget also asked for continuous frame ticks. A scroll view's wheel scroll,
which animates to the new offset, did nothing. Like the desktop widgets
editor, which also hosts several widgets on one surface, the widgets now share
the surface's manager. Instances are torn down while their surface still
exists, so the manager outlives them.

